# medya, the half in the Spanish-lexified clock, which attaches ADDITIVELY to
# the hour already named: "alas otso y medya ng gabi" == 20:30 and "alas
# kuwatro y medya ng hapon" == 16:30, both worked examples in the source.
# That is the opposite direction from the Continental-Germanic bare half, so
# the locale sets bare_half_past rather than bare_half_to.  The source spells
# the word med'ya/mediya; the apostrophe form is not shipped because the
# tokenizer would shear it.  medya has no Wiktionary Tagalog entry -- the
# citation is the worked clock examples alone.  en.wikipedia.org, "Date and time notation in the Philippines".
medya
mediya
